<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30066" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">murrĕus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">myrrhĕus, mur-rhĕus</span></b> ),
			a, um, adj.
		1. murra, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to
			myrrh</i>.—Esp. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>Anointed with myrrh, perfumed with myrrh</i> (<b>poet.</b>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">crinis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 3, 14, 22</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>Like myrrh, of the color of myrrh, yellowish</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Prop. 3, 10, 20</span></i> (4, 9, 22).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
